This data engineering internship delivered two initiatives: a production payment datamart that unifies digital-order and payment data into a validated, self-service source of truth, preserving retries, decline codes, split-tender payments, and authoritative settlement amounts; and an AI-assisted DFRAME onboarding workflow that generates compliant registration YAML and standardized feature descriptions. I strengthened skills in advanced SQL, Amazon Redshift, Datanet/BDT pipelines, Maestro/CDK, data lineage and validation, Python, Kiro CLI agents, Amazon Bedrock, IAM, APIs, Lambda-style registration workflows, and production testing. The work replaced fragile manual joins, unlocked payment-health metrics such as purchase success and initial-decline rates, achieved a 98.55% match rate for eligible paid successful orders, handled a 4 TB backfill safely, and made feature registration and discovery faster, more consistent, and easier to scale.

